<title>AUSTRALIA: SIA to buy one third of Ansett - paper.</title>
<headline>SIA to buy one third of Ansett - paper.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Airlines Ltd (SIA) is in preliminary talks to become an equal partner with News Corp Ltd and Air New Zealand Ltd in regional operator Ansett Holdings Ltd, the Australian Financial Review newspaper said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said SIA could pay between A$200 million and A$300 million to buy a one-third stake.</p>
<p>It said the inclusion of SIA would spread the considerable capital demands on Ansett which is undertaking a A$1.5 billion re-equipment programme. </p>
<p>The talks are at an early stage and sources in Singapore said it could take several months to conclude a deal.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
